+# ── Hot/cold expert residency (hot-experts patch, 2026-09-04) ─────────────────
+# With `--cpu-offload-params experts` the UVA offloader spills WHOLE per-layer expert
+# tensors first-come, so a layer is either 100% VRAM or 100% host and every routed read
+# in a spilled layer crosses PCIe. Routing is skewed (measured: the top-50% experts of a
+# layer take ~85% of decode routings), so instead: offload ALL expert tensors to host,
+# then at repack time gather each layer's most-used experts into a compact VRAM copy and
+# run the grouped GEMM twice — hot from VRAM, cold from the host tensor — into one
+# output buffer. Needs no kernel change: moe_align_block_size(ignore_invalid_experts=True)
+# with an expert_map emits local ids for one subset only, and the kernel writes only the
+# rows it is given.
+#   VLLM_R4D_HOT_PROFILE=/path.json  {"layers": {"<idx>": {"ranked": [expert ids, most
+#                                     used first], "counts": [...]}}}
+#   VLLM_R4D_HOT_GB=<float>          per-rank VRAM budget (GB, 1e9) for hot expert weights,
+#                                     spent globally on the highest-count (layer, expert)
+#                                     pairs — layers with flatter routing get fewer slots.
+#
+# ── Dynamic LRU expert cache (k1, 2026-09-04) ────────────────────────────────
+# The static hot set spends its slots on globally-frequent experts, but a single
+# generation's working set is per-prompt: measured on captured production routing
+# (k1/LOCALITY.md), one generation touches a median 320 distinct experts per layer while
+# the 15 GB set holds 257, and the static set misses 23.3% of distinct-per-step routings
+# where a per-layer LRU over the SAME slots misses 4.7% (-88% of cold PCIe bytes).
+# So: keep the compact VRAM buffers exactly as they are and make their contents mutable.
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU=1                   enable (default 0 = the static behaviour above)
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU_THRESH=<float>      skip inserts when a step routes more than this
+#                                     fraction of the slots (prefill chunks and wide
+#                                     batches read through instead of thrashing the cache)
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU_MAX_INSERTS=<int>   hard cap on inserts per layer per forward
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU_CHUNKS / _LANES     gather grid
+#   R4D_LRU_LIB=/path/librlu.so      the HIP kernels (k1/lru/)
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU_FUSE=1              one kernel for the manager AND both
+#                                     moe_align_block_size outputs: 6 launches per layer
+#                                     -> 2. Needs a librlu.so that exports r4d_lru_fused.
+#   VLLM_R4D_LRU_FUSE_MAX=<int>      fall back to the separate calls above this many
+#                                     (token, k) slots (prefill is not dispatch-bound)
+# Two kernels run per layer per forward, ahead of moe_align_block_size, both pure device
+# work with no host sync so the whole thing is HIP-graph capturable: only the CONTENTS of
+# table/map_cold/slot buffers change between replays, never a pointer.
